From 80fd8f4af7c84c444093c9485fbdb766da7ee25e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diogo Casteluber Laass <4793368+iowaz@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 19:47:41 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] PackagePartitions: Include the build time in the upgrade
 fingerprint

PackagePartitions.FINGERPRINT digests the partition fingerprints and
ro.build.version.incremental. The package manager compares it with the
value saved in packages.xml to decide whether the system was upgraded,
and names the package parser cache after it.

klimt reports its stock Xiaomi build identity, so all of those values
stay the same from one build to the next. A dirty flash of a new build
would then not count as an upgrade, and the parser cache of the old
system would be reused for the new one.

Add ro.build.date.utc to the digest. It is the real build time of every
build, so each new system build is an upgrade again. Apps don't see the
digest; the reported fingerprints and properties are unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 core/java/android/content/pm/PackagePartitions.java | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/core/java/android/content/pm/PackagePartitions.java b/core/java/android/content/pm/PackagePartitions.java
index da3b68ecf789..d03cbbe0abe3 100644
--- a/core/java/android/content/pm/PackagePartitions.java
+++ b/core/java/android/content/pm/PackagePartitions.java
@@ -126,12 +126,15 @@ public class PackagePartitions {
      */
     @NonNull
     private static String getFingerprint() {
-        final String[] digestProperties = new String[SYSTEM_PARTITIONS.size() + 1];
+        final String[] digestProperties = new String[SYSTEM_PARTITIONS.size() + 2];
         for (int i = 0; i < SYSTEM_PARTITIONS.size(); i++) {
             final String partitionName = SYSTEM_PARTITIONS.get(i).getName();
             digestProperties[i] = "ro." + partitionName + ".build.fingerprint";
         }
         digestProperties[SYSTEM_PARTITIONS.size()] = "ro.build.version.incremental";
+        // The fingerprints and incremental can stay the same across builds (a device may report its
+        // stock build identity), so the build time marks each new system build as an upgrade.
+        digestProperties[SYSTEM_PARTITIONS.size() + 1] = "ro.build.date.utc";
         return SystemProperties.digestOf(digestProperties);
     }
 
